{"clause_id": "c261", "issues": [
  {"issue": "'Purchase Price' is defined only for loans required to be repurchased 'pursuant to Section 2.02 hereof' or purchased under Section 4.21, yet Section 2.03 and the definition of 'Mortgage Loans' both require payment of the Purchase Price on repurchases arising under the Mortgage Loan Purchase Agreement and Bring Down Agreements. The definition's stated scope does not cover the repurchases the Agreement elsewhere contemplates.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34},
  {"issue": "The clause reads 'reduced by any portion of the Servicing Fee, Servicing Advances and Advances payable to the purchaser of the Mortgage Loan plus and (iii) any costs and damages', with a stray 'plus and' that leaves the relation between the deduction and item (iii) unclear. The predatory-lending damages component is also left at large as 'any costs and damages (if any) incurred by the Trust'.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}]},
